1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,963
Diwali is three weeks away, and every
sweet shop in Bengaluru is shouting.

2
00:00:05,263 --> 00:00:06,561
Laddoo Lab is tiny.

3
00:00:06,561 --> 00:00:09,489
How can it be heard, and
sell more this month?

4
00:00:10,039 --> 00:00:13,672
Zoya picks two tools:
advertising and sales promotion.

5
00:00:14,323 --> 00:00:16,251
Dev makes the festive ad.

6
00:00:16,251 --> 00:00:18,447
Arjun plans the festive offer.

7
00:00:18,797 --> 00:00:21,283
The ad gives people a reason to buy.

8
00:00:21,283 --> 00:00:24,073
The offer gives them a reason to buy now.

9
00:00:24,423 --> 00:00:28,781
Both carry one message: the healthy
tiffin sweet, now for Diwali too.

10
00:00:29,431 --> 00:00:31,271
First, what is advertising?

11
00:00:31,571 --> 00:00:36,571
Kotler and Armstrong call it any paid
form of non-personal presentation

12
00:00:36,571 --> 00:00:41,926
and promotion of ideas, goods or
services, by an identified sponsor.

13
00:00:42,276 --> 00:00:44,287
Paid means you buy the space.

14
00:00:44,287 --> 00:00:47,499
Non-personal means it talks
to many people at once.

15
00:00:47,499 --> 00:00:49,803
And everyone knows who is speaking.

16
00:00:50,153 --> 00:00:52,021
Sales promotion is different.

17
00:00:52,021 --> 00:00:55,815
It means short-term incentives
to encourage buying, right now.

18
00:00:56,465 --> 00:00:58,455
Every ad needs a clear job.

19
00:00:58,455 --> 00:00:59,857
Kotler names three.

20
00:01:00,207 --> 00:01:01,107
Inform.

21
00:01:00,904 --> 00:01:02,794
Tell people something new.

22
00:01:02,794 --> 00:01:05,677
Laddoo Lab now makes a festive gift box.

23
00:01:06,028 --> 00:01:06,928
Persuade.

24
00:01:06,808 --> 00:01:08,873
Give a reason to choose you.

25
00:01:08,873 --> 00:01:11,195
No refined sugar, made by Nani.

26
00:01:11,545 --> 00:01:12,445
Remind.

27
00:01:12,172 --> 00:01:13,785
Keep the brand in mind.

28
00:01:13,785 --> 00:01:16,612
A poster at the school
gate, every morning.

29
00:01:17,262 --> 00:01:19,239
Now watch six weeks of sales.

30
00:01:19,589 --> 00:01:21,034
Weeks one and two.

31
00:01:21,034 --> 00:01:22,095
Normal sales.

32
00:01:22,445 --> 00:01:24,230
Week three, the ad starts.

33
00:01:24,230 --> 00:01:27,287
Sales rise slowly, as more
parents hear about it.

34
00:01:27,637 --> 00:01:30,152
Weeks four and five, the festive offer.

35
00:01:30,152 --> 00:01:33,010
Buy two six-packs, get
a mini gift pack free.

36
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:34,320
Sales jump.

37
00:01:34,320 --> 00:01:37,651
Many families try Laddoo
Lab for the first time.

38
00:01:38,001 --> 00:01:39,896
Week six, the offer ends.

39
00:01:39,896 --> 00:01:41,123
Sales drop back.

40
00:01:41,473 --> 00:01:42,931
But not all the way.

41
00:01:42,931 --> 00:01:46,420
The ad and the new buyers
keep sales higher than before.

42
00:01:47,070 --> 00:01:49,064
Advertising builds the reason.

43
00:01:49,064 --> 00:01:50,807
Promotion gives the push.

44
00:01:51,507 --> 00:01:55,090
Arjun has many sales promotion
tools to choose from.

45
00:01:55,440 --> 00:01:56,340
Samples.

46
00:01:56,198 --> 00:01:58,227
Free tastes at three shops.

47
00:01:58,577 --> 00:01:59,477
Coupons.

48
00:01:59,347 --> 00:02:02,028
A discount code for the online shop.

49
00:02:02,378 --> 00:02:03,278
Premiums.

50
00:02:03,109 --> 00:02:06,632
A free gift with a purchase,
like the mini gift pack.

51
00:02:06,982 --> 00:02:08,910
And point of purchase displays.

52
00:02:08,910 --> 00:02:11,885
A bright stand right next
to the billing counter.

53
00:02:12,535 --> 00:02:14,503
Where do we see this at work today?

54
00:02:14,853 --> 00:02:15,753
Inform.

55
00:02:15,572 --> 00:02:19,058
A phone maker runs ads
to launch its new model.

56
00:02:19,408 --> 00:02:20,308
Remind.

57
00:02:20,057 --> 00:02:24,316
A cold drink brand runs ads every
summer, so you don't forget it.

58
00:02:24,666 --> 00:02:25,566
Coupons.

59
00:02:25,391 --> 00:02:29,551
A food delivery app gives a
discount code on your first order.

60
00:02:29,901 --> 00:02:30,801
Displays.

61
00:02:30,592 --> 00:02:34,554
A supermarket puts snacks near the
billing counter, where you wait.

62
00:02:35,204 --> 00:02:37,312
But can ads and offers go wrong?

63
00:02:37,312 --> 00:02:38,212
Yes.

64
00:02:38,136 --> 00:02:39,190
The good side.

65
00:02:39,190 --> 00:02:41,783
New people hear about you, and try you.

66
00:02:42,133 --> 00:02:43,241
The hard side.

67
00:02:43,241 --> 00:02:46,320
Too many offers teach
people to wait for deals.

68
00:02:46,320 --> 00:02:48,438
And some ads stretch the truth.

69
00:02:48,788 --> 00:02:51,878
Dev wants to write,
lowest price in Bengaluru.

70
00:02:51,878 --> 00:02:53,912
Zoya asks, can we prove it?

71
00:02:53,912 --> 00:02:54,812
No.

72
00:02:54,366 --> 00:02:55,333
So it goes.

73
00:02:55,683 --> 00:03:01,397
In India, the Advertising Standards
Council, set up in 1985, says ads must

74
00:03:01,397 --> 00:03:03,338
be honest and truthful.

75
00:03:03,338 --> 00:03:05,030
Anyone can complain.

76
00:03:05,380 --> 00:03:06,280
The lesson?

77
00:03:06,259 --> 00:03:10,006
Use offers for a push, but
let the product be the reason.

78
00:03:10,656 --> 00:03:11,580
Quick check.

79
00:03:11,580 --> 00:03:15,800
Buy two six-packs, get a mini gift
pack free, for two weeks only.

80
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:16,829
What is this?

81
00:03:18,729 --> 00:03:19,962
Sales promotion!

82
00:03:19,962 --> 00:03:22,345
A short-term incentive to buy now.

83
00:03:22,945 --> 00:03:23,954
So, remember.

84
00:03:24,254 --> 00:03:28,362
Advertising is paid, non-personal
and from a known sponsor.

85
00:03:28,362 --> 00:03:30,909
It informs, persuades and reminds.

86
00:03:31,259 --> 00:03:36,809
Sales promotion is a short-term push:
samples, coupons, premiums and displays.

87
00:03:37,159 --> 00:03:38,649
Ads build the reason.

88
00:03:38,649 --> 00:03:40,140
Offers give the push.

89
00:03:40,740 --> 00:03:44,322
Next time: personal selling,
and Arjun's big shop pitch.
